<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7471" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphīsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ŏs</span></b> ) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphissus</span></b> ,
		i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κηφῖσις</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κηφισσός</span>.
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river in Phocis and Bœotia</i>, now <i>Cephisso</i>, <i>Gaurio</i>, or <i>Gerios</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 7,
				349</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 3, 175</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 7,
				12</span></i>, §§ 26 and 27; <i>as
				river-god</i>, <i>father of Narcissus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3,
				343</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 7, 340</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphīsĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphissĭ-us</span></b> ,
				i, m., = Narcissus, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3,
				351</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cē-phīsis</span></b> 
			or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphissis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj. fem.</i>,
				<i>of Cephisus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">undas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 369</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river on the west side of Athens</i>, <i>emptying into the Saronic Gulf</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7,
				388</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphīsĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>name of a small
				district of Altica</i>, <i>abounding in
			springs</i>, <i><span class="en">Gell. 1, 2, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">18, 10, 1</span></i>; and of
				<i>a fountain</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 7,
				11, § 24</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphīsĭăs</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēphissĭas</span></b> ),
			ădis, <i>adj. fem.</i>, <i>of Cephisus</i>: ora, <i>the banks of
				the Attic Cephisus</i>, where Procrustes had his abode, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7,
				438</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
